WEBVTT

00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:02.388
Diamond rings weren't always a must.

00:00:02.398 --> 00:00:04.974
Before World War Two, only one in

00:00:04.984 --> 00:00:08.249
ten American engagement
rings had a diamond.

00:00:08.259 --> 00:00:10.861
In 1938, with sales crushed by the

00:00:10.871 --> 00:00:14.212
Depression, De Beers hired outside help.

00:00:14.312 --> 00:00:17.102
Its marketing even told men how much

00:00:17.112 --> 00:00:17.756
to spend:

00:00:17.766 --> 00:00:20.249
by the 1980s, two months' salary.

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:22.147
So how did the diamond ring catch

00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:22.701
on?

00:00:22.711 --> 00:00:25.427
Four words written in 1947 by ad

00:00:25.437 --> 00:00:27.418
writer Frances Gerety:

00:00:27.428 --> 00:00:29.361
a diamond is forever.

00:00:29.472 --> 00:00:31.772
Gerety herself never married.
